      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry oxygen-free argon (Schlenk) or nitrogen (glove box), a benzene (10 mL) solution of cubane-type methylidene complex 1 (0.209 g, 0.14 mmol) in a 20 mL Schlenk flask with a Young valve was frozen in liquid nitrogen and pumped to exclude N2. The solution was warmed to room temperature and back-filled with CO (1 atm). The reaction was rapid; within 30 min the colorless solution turned yellow. After removal of the solvent under vacuum, the residue was extracted with hexane. Slow evaporation under reduced pressure gave 2 as a white powder (0.194 g, 0.12 mmol, 86% isolated yield). Single crystals of 2·0.5C6H6 as pale yellow blocks were grown by recrystallization from benzene at room temperature.",
        "reagents": [
